☁️ 6. How to implement in AWS
🔥 Step 1: Create S3 bucket
aws s3 mb s3://velero-backups
🔥 Step 2: Create IAM user

Give permissions:

S3 full access
EC2 snapshot
🔥 Step 3: Install Velero
velero install \
  --provider aws \
  --plugins velero/velero-plugin-for-aws:v1.8.0 \
  --bucket velero-backups \
  --secret-file ./credentials-velero
🔥 Step 4: Verify
velero backup-location get
☁️ 7. How to implement in Azure (what you did)
🔥 Step 1: Create storage account
az storage account create ...
🔥 Step 2: Create container
az storage container create --name velero-backups
🔥 Step 3: Create service principal
az ad sp create-for-rbac
🔥 Step 4: Install Velero
velero install \
  --provider azure \
  --bucket velero-backups \
  --backup-location-config resourceGroup=velero-rg,storageAccount=velerostorage
🔥 Step 5: Verify
velero backup-location get

👉 Must be:

Available ✅
